## Made
### Code
My wakapi instance says I have a pitiful 5 hours and 28 minutes of code time for the
entire month :(

What tiny little bit I did was largely on the game project I wrote about last month, which
I am still excited about but need to actually buckle down and work on to at least get it
to a very basic vertical slice/playtestable version.

### Not Code
I built a lot of furniture this month. I have a bunch of friends all moving into new
places (tis the season), so I spent a good few weekends carting around heavy things and
putting together assorted beds/wardrobes/etc.

# Stuff I Didn't Do
* Once again, I did not finish the draft of the short story I've been working on. I'll
come by and noodle on it every few days, but it's in a bit of a rut at the moment. I think
I just need to push through and get *something* done so that I can start editing.
* Similar thing with the game idea as mentioned above: I've at least started on the
project (and to my credit have a pretty extensive design doc written out), but code wise
it is slim pickings.

# Stuff I'm Gonna Do in April
* Now that I'm back into the swing of things with the whole "having a job" thing, and with
a 4 day holiday weekend coming up, I'm planning to really power through a good chunk of
the secret game project. My goal is to get it to such a point that I can start to dogfood
it with friends at the end of the month, which includes a fully working basic server
implementation and some sort of very basic client (almost certainly just a webpage). I'm
excited to actually see if the idea has merit, and the good news is that if it dosen't one
of the pieces that I've already begun working on is just neat on its own, game or not.
* With the weather finally *finally* getting better, that means it's time to start
cranking my kilometers back up. For starters I'm aiming at 30k per week, maybe 35 by the
end of the month, but with a focus on my form for at least one run per week.
* In concert with the above, I want to do a better job with my diet in April. I tended to
reach for off the shelf pre-made stuff in March largely because my calendar suddenly went
from very empty to very full, but even when trying to not eat total junk stuff that comes
out of a plastic bag isn't ideal. I've got plenty of vegetarian staples that I can cook
without really batting an eye, so I want to really get myself in the habit of reaching for
that instead of yet another reheated pasta.

Short and sweet this month! Here's to an April filled with sun (*finally*) and runs!
